://www.cvinyl.com/labelguides/verve.php","https://londonjazzcollector.wordpress.com/record-labels-guide/8-verve/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/52056/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"52056","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:52056","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/52056-Asthmatic-Kitty","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/750/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"750","image":"https://i.discogs.com/l7MqdVik3dZV0Vxh1EPMGDz95ydeYSmjPKQjdwDc7uA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc1MC0x/NjE1MDQyNjg5LTc3/NDMucG5n.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/mAQvNiy2JcCbwtfQ5KDAxHhxDCI1BZ6bi5lp60iNvD8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc1MC0x/NjE1MDQyNjg5LTc3/NDMucG5n.jpeg","profile":"Multinational label, started by [a4812584] in the early 1970s as an independent label based in London, UK. \n[b]Label Code: LC 3098 / LC 03098[/b]\nThe record company [l26760] and subsidiaries which used the Virgin brand was sold to [l118508] Plc on 1 June 1992, the various Virgin trademarks however remained the property of [l326037], since 2012 the imprint has been licensed from [l326037] and is used by various companies that form part of the [l38404].\n\nIn the UK and most of Europe Virgin was distributed by EMI from 1 August 1992 and the EMI boxed catalogue numbering and barcode, price codes date from them. It was distributed in Germany by BMG until 1 August 1993 and the Benelux nations until mid-1994.\n\nIn North America, Virgin and associated labels were distributed by Atlantic/WEA until the same date, whereupon they moved to Capitol. Again, any EMI catalogue numbering dates to after that.\n\n[b]Please note, many Virgin issues also carry an EMI logo. This is not a label and EMI should not be added as a label, it instead indicates that Virgin was part of the EMI Group.[/b]\n\nThe Virgin disc label designs/logos:\n[a=Roger Dean (4)] was the designer of the original famous Virgin label with snakes and dragons.\n\nFor LP's following designs were used:\n1973-1974: white Roger Dean label\n1974-1976: coloured Roger Dean label [rim text was added at some point in 1975]\n1975: fawn & mauve Roger Dean label (V2037 to V2044 and some older reissues)\n1975-1976: red twin label with outer white ring\n1975-1976: green twin label with outer white ring\n1976-1978: green twin label (without outer white ring)\n1976-1977: red twin label (without outer white ring)\n1977-1978: blue label with double Virgin writing logo (V2086 to ??)\n1978-1987: green/red alternative label (Side 1 / Side 2)\n1987-xxxx: grey-white label\n\nThe fawn & mauve Dean label should have replaced the coloured Dean label in summer 1975 but has been used only a very short time. The fawn & mauve Dean label hasn't been used outside UK.\nThe red and green label with white outer ring replaced the fawn & mauve Dean label. It has been used in the UK a very short time only, and can also be found on Virgin albums outside the UK. \nThe green twin label (without outer white ring) has been used originally in 1976 but it is also available on reissues of older releases. In UK it has been used until 1978, but in other countries (e.g. Japan, Spain) there are records up to 1982 with this label. During this period, a few titles were pressed with a red twin label (without outer white ring).\nThe blue label with double Virgin writing logo is mostly found on single releases but it has also been used on a few albums.\nThe use of the green/red labels ended in 1987 in the UK, but in other countries it has been used longer (Spain until 1990, Germany until 1988).\nThe grey-white label was introduced in the UK in 1987 and a few months later in other countries, too (1988).\n\nFor 7\" releases following designs were used:\n1974-1975: black-white Dean label / white Dean label\n1976: blue twin label\n1976-1978: blue label with double Virgin writing logo\n1978-1987: green/red alternative label\n1987-xxx: silver label\n\nIn some countries the white or the black-white Dean label was longer in use (Germany, 1977). Spain was the only country that used the coloured Dean label on singles (instead of the white or black-white Dean label).\nThe blue twin label (which has never been used for albums) was issued in UK only.\nThe blue label with double Virgin writing logo was used from 1976 until 1978 in the UK. In some countries it was longer in use (Spain, 1979).\n\nOn 12\"s the following designs exist:\n1978 - 1987: green/red alternative label\n1988 - xxxx: grey-white label\n\nCD label designs:\nOlder CD's normally had a blue label (a kind of light blue layer on the silver disc) because the producers had problems with the printing on the blank silver surface.\nSome of the later editions have silver labels with red printing. \nNewer editions have black printing.\n\nOVED mid-price catalog numbers were introduced in July 1981, starting with OVED 1. \n\nFor unofficial releases, please use [l136191].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:750","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":26760,"name":"Virgin Records Ltd."},"sublabels":[{"id":1487444,"name":"*VF Version Française"},{"id":1517522,"name":"1+1 Free"},{"id":4484077,"name":"4 Track EP"},{"id":348091,"name":"Ambient Series"},{"id":2408620,"name":"Betafish Music"},{"id":702688,"name":"Brilliant Eighties"},{"id":40109,"name":"Clubtone (2)"},{"id":558681,"name":"Compact Price (2)"},{"id":668692,"name":"Crucial Cuts"},{"id":29236,"name":"DEP International"},{"id":1606,"name":"Freestyle Dust"},{"id":1022575,"name":"Front Line (2)"},{"id":36314,"name":"Hi-Rise Recordings"},{"id":1161417,"name":"Hut Records (5)"},{"id":4562,"name":"Innocent"},{"id":1412296,"name":"Les Grandes Musiques De Films Virgin"},{"id":675,"name":"Melankolic"},{"id":3530002,"name":"Memories Are Made Of This"},{"id":11160,"name":"Metal Beat"},{"id":4269,"name":"More Protein"},{"id":785381,"name":"Nuke (2)"},{"id":532439,"name":"Nyman at 60"},{"id":91204,"name":"Pointblank"},{"id":2058703,"name":"Power Ballads (3)"},{"id":231,"name":"Quigley Records"},{"id":786038,"name":"Sampled"},{"id":299,"name":"Science"},{"id":994001,"name":"Sheep Records (3)"},{"id":251281,"name":"Tangerine Dream Definitive Edition"},{"id":432189,"name":"The Invisible Series"},{"id":1364479,"name":"The Love Album"},{"id":887352,"name":"The Remastered Series (2)"},{"id":1383731,"name":"The Royal Collection Of Mewar"},{"id":381204,"name":"The Virgin Mid-Price Range."},{"id":439694,"name":"Themes (Simple Minds)"},{"id":783592,"name":"This Is... (2)"},{"id":7325,"name":"Variation"},{"id":121731,"name":"VENTURE"},{"id":623034,"name":"Virgin (4)"},{"id":26520,"name":"Virgin America"},{"id":345330,"name":"Virgin And Palace Video Distribution."},{"id":548873,"name":"Virgin Best Selections 30"},{"id":72127,"name":"Virgin Chattering Classics"},{"id":323586,"name":"Virgin Choice Cuts"},{"id":3368262,"name":"Virgin Comedy Club"},{"id":17787,"name":"Virgin Dance"},{"id":3139226,"name":"Virgin Hits"},{"id":22998,"name":"Virgin International"},{"id":1121070,"name":"Virgin Liberty"},{"id":1294643,"name":"Virgin Megastore (2)"},{"id":734328,"name":"Virgin Mex"},{"id":1544087,"name":"Virgin Mexico"},{"id":168456,"name":"Virgin Movie Music"},{"id":26063,"name":"Virgin Music"},{"id":45391,"name":"Virgin Music (Belgium)"},{"id":45047,"name":"Virgin Music Belgium"},{"id":302407,"name":"Virgin Music Belgium NV"},{"id":78298,"name":"Virgin Music Canada"},{"id":3186806,"name":"Virgin Music In America"},{"id":568634,"name":"Virgin Music Publishing"},{"id":17742,"name":"Virgin Music Video"},{"id":108701,"name":"Virgin Records"},{"id":301324,"name":"Virgin Records España, S.A."},{"id":2349556,"name":"Virgin Records France"},{"id":77406,"name":"Virgin Records Sweden Ab"},{"id":7436,"name":"Virgin Underground"},{"id":169831,"name":"Virgin Universal"},{"id":326327,"name":"Virgin Value"},{"id":17769